PN,31702
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786234686
OL,3,C'I want my son back': Mother's fight
OL,4,Cto free son jailed in 2005 over phone
OL,5,Ctheft
OL,7,FThen 18 years old, he was one of the
OL,8,Ffirst prisoners to be given an IPP,
OL,9,Fwhich was introduced in the same year.
OL,11,FAn IPP means offenders have a minimum
OL,12,Fterm to their sentence, but no
OL,13,Fautomatic end date.
OL,15,FEven when released, they are placed on
OL,16,Findefinite licence, meaning they are
OL,17,Fnever truly free.
OL,19,FShaun served eight years from 2006 to
OL,20,F2014 before he was first released, but
OL,21,Fhe has since been recalled five times.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
